# Reference list of the environment variables the shelfscan CLI reads.
#
# This is NOT a file the program loads. Nothing in this codebase parses a
# .env file -- the CLI reads Platform.environment and nothing else. Copying
# this to .env and filling it in has no effect and produces no error, so
# set the variables in your shell (or your run configuration) instead:
#
#   PowerShell:  $env:IGDB_CLIENT_ID = '...'
#   bash:        export IGDB_CLIENT_ID=...
#
# Every name below is shown blank, and blank is exactly what unset is: the
# CLI reads them all through one accessor that treats a set-but-empty value
# as absent. So `export` of this file's lines wholesale leaves every default
# in place rather than breaking the local run.
#
# The Flutter app ignores this file entirely: per decision 0011 it keeps keys
# in the OS keychain (flutter_secure_storage), never on disk in the repo.

# --- IGDB resolution (pipeline stage 3) ----------------------------- #
# Both come from a Twitch application:
# https://api-docs.igdb.com/#getting-started
# Without them `scan` skips the resolve stage and leaves games unresolved;
# `resolve` refuses to run, since resolving is its entire purpose.
IGDB_CLIENT_ID=
IGDB_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- TMDB resolution, for film and anime rows (pipeline stage 3) ---- #
# The API Read Access Token from https://www.themoviedb.org/settings/api --
# NOT the v3 "API Key", which TMDB accepts only as a query parameter and
# which would therefore sit in every URL an error or a log quotes.
#
# A THIRD credential, and it is optional in the strongest sense: without it
# a film or anime row is keyless -- the title read off the filename, CSV yes,
# .xcoll no -- exactly as a game row is without the two variables above.
# Nothing else about the run changes, and games are unaffected either way.
#
# One token, two endpoints. Films and anime films are searched in TMDB's film
# search; anime series in its tv search. Only the film search has ever been
# run against the live service, and films came back -- what that does not
# tell you is how well it answers the release names you actually have, since
# a few public titles on one evening is the whole of the measurement. The tv
# search has never been called at all, so anime rows are wiring rather than a
# result. And no .xcoll holding a film or an anime has been imported into a
# collection manager here. Read both kinds at review the way you read any
# other row.
SHELFSCAN_TMDB_TOKEN=

# --- Vision provider ------------------------------------------------ #
# Needed only for `--provider anthropic` (cloud, an explicit opt-in on
# desktop). The default local provider needs no key.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional overrides for the default local provider (`--provider ollama`).
# Blank means "use the built-in default": qwen3-vl:8b-instruct at
# http://localhost:11434. That model is the one tested on this route; it is
# NOT the model this project's figures were measured on. Those are
# qwen2.5vl:7b's, which was the built-in default until 2026-09-04 -- name it
# here to reproduce them. These two were the file's only commented-out
# entries, because a blank one used to be taken as a value and an empty base
# URL failed minutes into the run blaming Ollama (T-0080).
SHELFSCAN_OLLAMA_MODEL=
SHELFSCAN_OLLAMA_URL=

# A second LOCAL model that re-reads every photo (`--fallback`); it can never
# select a cloud one, and it doubles the vision cost of the run.
SHELFSCAN_OLLAMA_FALLBACK_MODEL=

# Whole seconds one vision call is given, for whichever provider is in use.
# Blank is 120 s -- ~3.5x the slowest read measured here, and below the one
# model this project measured above it (qwen2.5vl:32b, ~360 s per hi-res
# photo for want of VRAM). Raise it only for a model that slow. 1 to 1800;
# anything else is refused rather than replaced by the default, because a
# raise that did not take looks exactly like the timeout it was meant to fix.
SHELFSCAN_VISION_TIMEOUT=

# Optional. Blank uses the provider's own default. Naming a model here also
# stops shelfscan stating a temperature -- the newer Claude families reject
# one -- so note which model produced any numbers you record. Current ids:
# platform.claude.com/docs models overview, or GET api.anthropic.com/v1/models.
SHELFSCAN_ANTHROPIC_MODEL=

# All three are needed by `--provider openai` / `--fallback openai`: any
# endpoint speaking the OpenAI /chat/completions API (Groq, OpenRouter,
# Mistral, GitHub Models, Cerebras, Gemini's compatibility endpoint). Setting
# them configures that endpoint but never selects it -- only the flag does,
# because your photos are uploaded there and free tiers are commonly funded
# by training on what is submitted to them.
# The base URL goes up to and including the version segment, e.g.
#   https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
#   https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
#   https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai
SHELFSCAN_OPENAI_BASE_URL=
SHELFSCAN_OPENAI_MODEL=
SHELFSCAN_OPENAI_API_KEY=
